{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b10b897d-96dd-5eb7-a0ca-0bc4d99f83cc",
    "name": "cloudf.one - Cloud Phone API",
    "description": "REST API for [cloudf.one](https://cloudf.one/?utm_source=postman&utm_medium=collection): real Android phones in Singapore on Singtel or M1 SIMs, rented by the day, week or month.\n\nThe phone panel runs DeviceFarmer STF 2.4.1 and this is its API, scoped to the phones on your account. This collection covers the endpoints we support; the full STF spec is at https://cloudf.one/api/v1/swagger.json, but its admin endpoints (groups, users, bookings) are restricted.\n\n**Auth:** log in, open your phone once, then go to cloudf.one/#!/settings > Access tokens and generate one. Set it as `accessToken`; it's sent as `Authorization: Bearer`. Tokens don't expire on a timer.\n\n**What the API doesn't do:** adb over the internet (the remoteConnect port isn't reachable from outside; a WireGuard tunnel is available on request), input injection or screenshots over REST (that's STF's websocket protocol), APK install (web UI or tunnelled adb), or credit top-ups (web only). No published rate limit; polling /devices every few seconds is fine.\n\nHuman docs: https://cloudf.one/developers",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
